
<Defs xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="rimworld DefsSchema.xsd" xmlns="rimworld">
    <!--
        Monster Extremists ideology meme ("All men should be drained, and all
        women should be transformed!"). Everything in this file is gated behind
        MayRequire Ideology: without the DLC none of these defs load, and the
        C# workers they reference are never instantiated.

        Contents:
        - Issue + three ascension precept varieties, all gated behind the
          Monster Extremists meme via requiredMemes (like vanilla's Blindsight
          rites): relaxed (admires the ascended, no judgment of non-momos),
          exalted (the original: ascended + baseliner social opinion thoughts),
          and strict (both thoughts at doubled values). Ascended = any Momo or
          tsugai-bonded pawn; baseliner = any adult humanlike who is neither —
          children are ignored.
        - Two rites of awakening (ritual precept + pattern + behavior + outcome),
          also gated behind the meme: the colonist rite transforms a willing
          colonist into the organiser's own monster xenotype; the captive rite
          transforms a prisoner/slave into a RANDOM monster xenotype and shakes
          her will, resistance and ideo certainty. A failed rite simply fizzles.
        - The meme itself, which requires one ascension variety plus both rites.
    -->

    <!-- ===================== Issue & ascension precepts ===================== -->

    <IssueDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_Issue_MonsterAscension</defName>
        <label>monster ascension</label>
        <iconPath>UI/Icons/Issues/Monsterise</iconPath>
    </IssueDef>

    <!-- Relaxed: the ascended are admired, but baseliners are left in peace —
         no negative opinions or moods toward non-momos at all. -->
    <PreceptDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_MonsterAscension_Relaxed</defName>
        <issue>ProjectMomo_Issue_MonsterAscension</issue>
        <label>relaxed</label>
        <description>Monsters and their bonded mates are admired as the vanguard of a beautiful transformation, but those content with baseline flesh are simply left to their own path — no scorn, no pressure.</description>
        <impact>Low</impact>
        <displayOrderInIssue>0</displayOrderInIssue>
        <displayOrderInImpact>100</displayOrderInImpact>
        <defaultSelectionWeight>1</defaultSelectionWeight>
        <conflictingMemes>
            <li>FleshPurity</li>
            <li>Transhumanist</li>
        </conflictingMemes>
        <associatedMemes>
            <li>ProjectMomo_Meme_MonsterExtremists</li>
        </associatedMemes>
        <requiredMemes>
            <li>ProjectMomo_Meme_MonsterExtremists</li>
        </requiredMemes>
        <comps>
            <li Class="PreceptComp_SituationalThought">
                <thought>ProjectMomo_MonsterExtremistAscendedRelaxed</thought>
                <thoughtStageDescriptions>
                    <li>Monster ascension (ascended)</li>
                </thoughtStageDescriptions>
            </li>
        </comps>
    </PreceptDef>

    <PreceptDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_MonsterAscension_Exalted</defName>
        <issue>ProjectMomo_Issue_MonsterAscension</issue>
        <label>exalted</label>
        <description>The baseline human form is a larval state, unworthy of respect. Women must be remade as monsters, and men must be claimed and drained by them. Only the ascended — monsters and their bonded mates — are truly worthy.</description>
        <impact>Medium</impact>
        <displayOrderInIssue>1</displayOrderInIssue>
        <displayOrderInImpact>100</displayOrderInImpact>
        <defaultSelectionWeight>1</defaultSelectionWeight>
        <conflictingMemes>
            <li>FleshPurity</li>
            <li>Transhumanist</li>
        </conflictingMemes>
        <associatedMemes>
            <li>ProjectMomo_Meme_MonsterExtremists</li>
        </associatedMemes>
        <requiredMemes>
            <li>ProjectMomo_Meme_MonsterExtremists</li>
        </requiredMemes>
        <comps>
            <li Class="PreceptComp_SituationalThought">
                <thought>ProjectMomo_MonsterExtremistAscended</thought>
                <thoughtStageDescriptions>
                    <li>Monster ascension (ascended)</li>
                </thoughtStageDescriptions>
            </li>
            <li Class="PreceptComp_SituationalThought">
                <thought>ProjectMomo_MonsterExtremistBaseliner</thought>
                <thoughtStageDescriptions>
                    <li>Monster ascension (baseliner)</li>
                </thoughtStageDescriptions>
            </li>
        </comps>
    </PreceptDef>

    <!-- Strict: the same judgment as exalted, but zealous — ascended admired
         twice as strongly, baseliners scorned twice as harshly. -->
    <PreceptDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_MonsterAscension_Strict</defName>
        <issue>ProjectMomo_Issue_MonsterAscension</issue>
        <label>strict</label>
        <description>The baseline human form is a stain to be scrubbed from the world. Women who refuse remaking and men who refuse claiming are worse than ignorant — they are cowards hoarding rotten flesh. Only the ascended — monsters and their bonded mates — deserve honor.</description>
        <impact>High</impact>
        <displayOrderInIssue>2</displayOrderInIssue>
        <displayOrderInImpact>100</displayOrderInImpact>
        <defaultSelectionWeight>1</defaultSelectionWeight>
        <conflictingMemes>
            <li>FleshPurity</li>
            <li>Transhumanist</li>
        </conflictingMemes>
        <associatedMemes>
            <li>ProjectMomo_Meme_MonsterExtremists</li>
        </associatedMemes>
        <requiredMemes>
            <li>ProjectMomo_Meme_MonsterExtremists</li>
        </requiredMemes>
        <comps>
            <li Class="PreceptComp_SituationalThought">
                <thought>ProjectMomo_MonsterExtremistAscendedStrict</thought>
                <thoughtStageDescriptions>
                    <li>Monster ascension (ascended)</li>
                </thoughtStageDescriptions>
            </li>
            <li Class="PreceptComp_SituationalThought">
                <thought>ProjectMomo_MonsterExtremistBaselinerStrict</thought>
                <thoughtStageDescriptions>
                    <li>Monster ascension (baseliner)</li>
                </thoughtStageDescriptions>
            </li>
        </comps>
    </PreceptDef>

    <!-- Opinion offsets come from mod settings (Thought_MonsterExtremistSocial):
         relaxed grants half the ascended opinion, strict grants double both
         opinions. The stage values below only mirror the resulting defaults
         for UI readouts that bypass OpinionOffset(). -->
    <ThoughtDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_MonsterExtremistAscendedRelaxed</defName>
        <thoughtClass>ProjectMomo.Thought_MonsterExtremistSocial</thoughtClass>
        <workerClass>ProjectMomo.ThoughtWorker_MonsterExtremistAscendedSocial</workerClass>
        <stages>
            <li>
                <label>ascended</label>
                <baseOpinionOffset>5</baseOpinionOffset>
            </li>
        </stages>
    </ThoughtDef>

    <ThoughtDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_MonsterExtremistAscended</defName>
        <thoughtClass>ProjectMomo.Thought_MonsterExtremistSocial</thoughtClass>
        <workerClass>ProjectMomo.ThoughtWorker_MonsterExtremistAscendedSocial</workerClass>
        <stages>
            <li>
                <label>ascended</label>
                <baseOpinionOffset>10</baseOpinionOffset>
            </li>
        </stages>
    </ThoughtDef>

    <ThoughtDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_MonsterExtremistAscendedStrict</defName>
        <thoughtClass>ProjectMomo.Thought_MonsterExtremistSocial</thoughtClass>
        <workerClass>ProjectMomo.ThoughtWorker_MonsterExtremistAscendedSocial</workerClass>
        <stages>
            <li>
                <label>ascended</label>
                <baseOpinionOffset>20</baseOpinionOffset>
            </li>
        </stages>
    </ThoughtDef>

    <ThoughtDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_MonsterExtremistBaseliner</defName>
        <thoughtClass>ProjectMomo.Thought_MonsterExtremistSocial</thoughtClass>
        <workerClass>ProjectMomo.ThoughtWorker_MonsterExtremistBaselinerSocial</workerClass>
        <stages>
            <li>
                <label>unascended baseliner</label>
                <baseOpinionOffset>-15</baseOpinionOffset>
            </li>
        </stages>
    </ThoughtDef>

    <ThoughtDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_MonsterExtremistBaselinerStrict</defName>
        <thoughtClass>ProjectMomo.Thought_MonsterExtremistSocial</thoughtClass>
        <workerClass>ProjectMomo.ThoughtWorker_MonsterExtremistBaselinerSocial</workerClass>
        <stages>
            <li>
                <label>unascended baseliner</label>
                <baseOpinionOffset>-30</baseOpinionOffset>
            </li>
        </stages>
    </ThoughtDef>

    <!-- ===================== Ritual speech interactions ===================== -->

    <InteractionDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_Speech_TransformRite</defName>
        <label>awakening rite speech</label>
        <workerClass>InteractionWorker</workerClass>
        <ignoreTimeSinceLastInteraction>True</ignoreTimeSinceLastInteraction>
        <symbol>Things/Mote/SpeechSymbols/Speech</symbol>
        <logRulesInitiator>
            <include><li>SpeechUtility</li></include>
            <rulesStrings>
                <li>r_logentry-&gt;[INITIATOR_nameDef] [spokeof] [speechtopic].</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;the beauty of the monster form</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;the joy of awakening</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;shedding the weakness of flesh</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;the Mamono Lord's gift</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;sisterhood among monsters</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;the sweetness of mana</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;leaving humanity behind</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;the bliss of transformation</li>
            </rulesStrings>
        </logRulesInitiator>
    </InteractionDef>

    <InteractionDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_Speech_TransformCaptiveRite</defName>
        <label>forced awakening speech</label>
        <workerClass>InteractionWorker</workerClass>
        <ignoreTimeSinceLastInteraction>True</ignoreTimeSinceLastInteraction>
        <symbol>Things/Mote/SpeechSymbols/Speech</symbol>
        <logRulesInitiator>
            <include><li>SpeechUtility</li></include>
            <rulesStrings>
                <li>r_logentry-&gt;[INITIATOR_nameDef] [spokeof] [speechtopic].</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;the gift bestowed on the unwilling</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;resistance melting into bliss</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;the mercy of monstrous rebirth</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;what she will become</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;the futility of clinging to old flesh</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;the monster sleeping within her</li>
                <li>speechtopic-&gt;gratitude she will one day feel</li>
            </rulesStrings>
        </logRulesInitiator>
    </InteractionDef>

    <!-- ===================== Ritual precepts ===================== -->

    <PreceptDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_Ritual_TransformColonist</defName>
        <label>rite of awakening</label>
        <description>A sacred rite in which a monster pours her mana into a willing sister, remaking her as a monster like herself. If the rite goes poorly, the mana fails to take hold and nothing happens.</description>
        <issue>Ritual</issue>
        <impact>Medium</impact>
        <iconPath>UI/Icons/Rituals/FreeMonsterise</iconPath>
        <preceptClass>Precept_Ritual</preceptClass>
        <ritualPatternBase>ProjectMomo_RitualPattern_TransformColonist</ritualPatternBase>
        <requiredMemes>
            <li>ProjectMomo_Meme_MonsterExtremists</li>
        </requiredMemes>
        <!-- No allowDuplicates: a single-purpose rite must be granted once, like
             vanilla's Execution/GladiatorDuel. Setting it true (as Scarification
             does) makes the ideo generator add the rite twice. -->
        <countsTowardsPreceptLimit>false</countsTowardsPreceptLimit>
        <selectionWeight>1.0</selectionWeight>
        <displayOrderInImpact>100</displayOrderInImpact>
    </PreceptDef>

    <PreceptDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_Ritual_TransformCaptive</defName>
        <label>rite of forced awakening</label>
        <description>A solemn rite in which a monster pours her mana into a prisoner or slave, willing or not, remaking her as a monster. If the rite goes poorly, the mana fails to take hold and nothing happens.</description>
        <issue>Ritual</issue>
        <impact>Medium</impact>
        <iconPath>UI/Icons/Rituals/ForceMonsterise</iconPath>
        <preceptClass>Precept_Ritual</preceptClass>
        <ritualPatternBase>ProjectMomo_RitualPattern_TransformCaptive</ritualPatternBase>
        <requiredMemes>
            <li>ProjectMomo_Meme_MonsterExtremists</li>
        </requiredMemes>
        <countsTowardsPreceptLimit>false</countsTowardsPreceptLimit>
        <selectionWeight>1.0</selectionWeight>
        <displayOrderInImpact>100</displayOrderInImpact>
    </PreceptDef>

    <!-- ===================== Ritual patterns ===================== -->

    <RitualPatternDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_RitualPattern_TransformColonist</defName>
        <alwaysStartAnytime>true</alwaysStartAnytime>
        <ritualObligationTargetFilter>RitualSpotIdeogramOrAltar</ritualObligationTargetFilter>
        <ritualTargetFilter>AltarIdeogramOrRitualSpot</ritualTargetFilter>
        <ritualBehavior>ProjectMomo_RitualBehavior_TransformColonist</ritualBehavior>
        <ritualOnlyForIdeoMembers>true</ritualOnlyForIdeoMembers>
        <ritualOutcomeEffect>ProjectMomo_RitualOutcome_TransformColonist</ritualOutcomeEffect>
        <tags>
            <li>ProjectMomo_TransformColonist</li>
        </tags>
    </RitualPatternDef>

    <RitualPatternDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_RitualPattern_TransformCaptive</defName>
        <alwaysStartAnytime>true</alwaysStartAnytime>
        <ritualObligationTargetFilter>RitualSpotIdeogramOrAltar</ritualObligationTargetFilter>
        <ritualTargetFilter>AltarIdeogramOrRitualSpot</ritualTargetFilter>
        <ritualBehavior>ProjectMomo_RitualBehavior_TransformCaptive</ritualBehavior>
        <ritualOnlyForIdeoMembers>false</ritualOnlyForIdeoMembers>
        <ritualOutcomeEffect>ProjectMomo_RitualOutcome_TransformCaptive</ritualOutcomeEffect>
        <tags>
            <li>ProjectMomo_TransformCaptive</li>
        </tags>
    </RitualPatternDef>

    <!-- ===================== Ritual behaviors ===================== -->

    <!-- Colonist rite: the corruptor escorts the willing convert to the ritual
         spot (scarification-style), then pours her mana in a speech while the
         convert lies in the ritual circle. -->
    <RitualBehaviorDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_RitualBehavior_TransformColonist</defName>
        <durationTicks>2500</durationTicks>
        <useVisualEffectsFromRoleIdIdeo>corruptor</useVisualEffectsFromRoleIdIdeo>
        <roles Inherit="False">
            <li Class="ProjectMomo.RitualRoleMomo">
                <label>corruptor</label>
                <id>corruptor</id>
                <maxCount>1</maxCount>
                <required>True</required>
                <missingDesc>a monster to lead the rite</missingDesc>
                <countsAsParticipant>False</countsAsParticipant>
                <allowChild>false</allowChild>
                <mustBeAbleToReachTarget>True</mustBeAbleToReachTarget>
            </li>
            <li Class="ProjectMomo.RitualRoleTransformableColonist">
                <label>convert</label>
                <id>convert</id>
                <maxCount>1</maxCount>
                <required>True</required>
                <missingDesc>the woman to awaken</missingDesc>
                <ignoreBleeding>true</ignoreBleeding>
                <countsAsParticipant>False</countsAsParticipant>
                <allowChild>false</allowChild>
            </li>
        </roles>
        <stages>
            <!-- Convert is taken -->
            <li Class="RitualStage_InteractWithRole">
                <targets>
                    <li>
                        <pawnId>corruptor</pawnId>
                        <targetId>convert</targetId>
                    </li>
                </targets>
                <defaultDuty>Spectate</defaultDuty>
                <essential>True</essential>
                <failTriggers>
                    <li Class="StageFailTrigger_TargetPawnUnreachable">
                        <takerId>corruptor</takerId>
                        <takeeId>convert</takeeId>
                        <desc>Convert is not reachable.</desc>
                    </li>
                    <li Class="StageFailTrigger_PawnAsleep">
                        <desc>escort asleep</desc>
                        <pawnId>corruptor</pawnId>
                    </li>
                </failTriggers>
                <endTriggers>
                    <li Class="StageEndTrigger_RolesArrived">
                        <roleIds>
                            <li>corruptor</li>
                        </roleIds>
                        <clearTag>true</clearTag>
                    </li>
                </endTriggers>
                <roleBehaviors>
                    <li>
                        <roleId>corruptor</roleId>
                        <dutyDef>DeliverPawnToCell</dutyDef>
                        <customPositions>
                            <li Class="RitualPosition_OnInteractionCell">
                                <offset>(-1,0,0)</offset>
                                <facing>South</facing>
                            </li>
                        </customPositions>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <roleId>convert</roleId>
                        <dutyDef>Idle</dutyDef>
                    </li>
                </roleBehaviors>
            </li>
            <!-- The pouring of mana -->
            <li>
                <defaultDuty>Spectate</defaultDuty>
                <essential>True</essential>
                <endTriggers>
                    <li Class="StageEndTrigger_DurationPercentage">
                        <percentage>1</percentage>
                    </li>
                </endTriggers>
                <roleBehaviors>
                    <li>
                        <roleId>corruptor</roleId>
                        <dutyDef>SpeakOnCellFacingSpectators</dutyDef>
                        <speakerInteraction>ProjectMomo_Speech_TransformRite</speakerInteraction>
                        <customPositions>
                            <li Class="RitualPosition_Lectern">
                                <maxDistanceToFocus>5</maxDistanceToFocus>
                            </li>
                            <li Class="RitualPosition_OnInteractionCell" />
                        </customPositions>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <roleId>convert</roleId>
                        <dutyDef>LayDownAwake</dutyDef>
                    </li>
                </roleBehaviors>
            </li>
        </stages>
    </RitualBehaviorDef>

    <!-- Captive rite: the corruptor escorts the prisoner/slave to the ritual
         focus (execution-style), then pours her mana over her. -->
    <RitualBehaviorDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_RitualBehavior_TransformCaptive</defName>
        <durationTicks>2500</durationTicks>
        <useVisualEffectsFromRoleIdIdeo>corruptor</useVisualEffectsFromRoleIdIdeo>
        <roles Inherit="False">
            <li Class="ProjectMomo.RitualRoleMomo">
                <label>corruptor</label>
                <id>corruptor</id>
                <maxCount>1</maxCount>
                <required>True</required>
                <missingDesc>a monster to lead the rite</missingDesc>
                <countsAsParticipant>False</countsAsParticipant>
                <allowChild>false</allowChild>
                <mustBeAbleToReachTarget>True</mustBeAbleToReachTarget>
            </li>
            <li Class="ProjectMomo.RitualRoleTransformableCaptive">
                <label>captive</label>
                <id>captive</id>
                <maxCount>1</maxCount>
                <required>True</required>
                <missingDesc>the captive to awaken</missingDesc>
                <ignoreBleeding>true</ignoreBleeding>
                <allowDowned>true</allowDowned>
                <removeFromAssignmentsOnDeath>false</removeFromAssignmentsOnDeath>
                <countsAsParticipant>False</countsAsParticipant>
                <allowChild>false</allowChild>
            </li>
        </roles>
        <stages>
            <!-- Captive is taken -->
            <li Class="RitualStage_InteractWithPrisoner">
                <defaultDuty>Spectate</defaultDuty>
                <endTriggers>
                    <li Class="StageEndTrigger_PawnDeliveredOrNotValid" />
                </endTriggers>
                <failTriggers>
                    <li Class="StageFailTrigger_TargetPawnUnreachable">
                        <takerId>corruptor</takerId>
                        <takeeId>captive</takeeId>
                        <desc>Captive is not reachable.</desc>
                    </li>
                    <li Class="StageFailTrigger_PawnAsleep">
                        <desc>escort asleep</desc>
                        <pawnId>corruptor</pawnId>
                    </li>
                </failTriggers>
                <roleBehaviors>
                    <li>
                        <roleId>corruptor</roleId>
                        <dutyDef>DeliverPawnToAltar</dutyDef>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <roleId>captive</roleId>
                        <dutyDef>Idle</dutyDef>
                    </li>
                </roleBehaviors>
            </li>
            <!-- The pouring of mana -->
            <li>
                <defaultDuty>Spectate</defaultDuty>
                <endTriggers>
                    <li Class="StageEndTrigger_DurationPercentage">
                        <percentage>1</percentage>
                    </li>
                </endTriggers>
                <roleBehaviors>
                    <li>
                        <roleId>corruptor</roleId>
                        <dutyDef>SpeakOnCellFacingSpectators</dutyDef>
                        <speakerInteraction>ProjectMomo_Speech_TransformCaptiveRite</speakerInteraction>
                        <customPositions>
                            <li Class="RitualPosition_OnInteractionCell" />
                        </customPositions>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <roleId>captive</roleId>
                        <dutyDef>LayDownAwake</dutyDef>
                    </li>
                </roleBehaviors>
            </li>
        </stages>
    </RitualBehaviorDef>

    <!-- ===================== Ritual outcomes ===================== -->

    <RitualOutcomeEffectDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_RitualOutcome_TransformColonist</defName>
        <description>If the rite goes well, the convert will be transformed into the corruptor's own monster xenotype. If it goes badly, the mana fails to take hold and nothing happens.</description>
        <workerClass>ProjectMomo.RitualOutcomeEffectWorker_TransformColonist</workerClass>
        <givesDevelopmentPoints>false</givesDevelopmentPoints>
        <comps>
            <li Class="RitualOutcomeComp_RoomStat">
                <label>room impressiveness</label>
                <statDef>Impressiveness</statDef>
                <curve>
                    <points>
                        <li>0,  0</li>
                        <li>50,  0.1</li>
                        <li>120, 0.2</li>
                    </points>
                </curve>
            </li>
            <li Class="RitualOutcomeComp_ParticipantCount">
                <label>participant count</label>
                <curve>
                    <points>
                        <li>(1,  0.0)</li>
                        <li>(5,  0.3)</li>
                        <li>(10, 0.4)</li>
                    </points>
                </curve>
            </li>
        </comps>
        <outcomeChances>
            <li>
                <label>Fumbled</label>
                <chance>0.05</chance>
                <description>The {0} was a humiliating muddle: the corruptor stumbled over the rite, the mana scattered like sparks, and the convert was left waiting on the cold floor.</description>
                <positivityIndex>-2</positivityIndex>
            </li>
            <li>
                <label>Fizzled</label>
                <chance>0.15</chance>
                <description>The {0} was weak. The mana flickered and dimmed before it could take root, and the rite quietly fell apart.</description>
                <positivityIndex>-1</positivityIndex>
            </li>
            <li>
                <label>Beautiful</label>
                <chance>0.6</chance>
                <description>The {0} was beautiful. The mana poured in without pause, and the convert's old body melted gracefully into her new, monstrous form.</description>
                <positivityIndex>1</positivityIndex>
            </li>
            <li>
                <label>Transcendent</label>
                <chance>0.2</chance>
                <description>The {0} was transcendent. The mana sang as it remade her, and the convert rose reborn in radiant, monstrous glory.</description>
                <positivityIndex>2</positivityIndex>
            </li>
        </outcomeChances>
    </RitualOutcomeEffectDef>

    <RitualOutcomeEffectDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_RitualOutcome_TransformCaptive</defName>
        <description>If the rite goes well, the captive will be transformed into a random monster xenotype, and her will, resistance and certainty in her old beliefs will be shaken. If it goes badly, the mana fails to take hold and nothing happens.</description>
        <workerClass>ProjectMomo.RitualOutcomeEffectWorker_TransformCaptive</workerClass>
        <givesDevelopmentPoints>false</givesDevelopmentPoints>
        <comps>
            <li Class="RitualOutcomeComp_RoomStat">
                <label>room impressiveness</label>
                <statDef>Impressiveness</statDef>
                <curve>
                    <points>
                        <li>0,  0</li>
                        <li>50,  0.1</li>
                        <li>120, 0.2</li>
                    </points>
                </curve>
            </li>
            <li Class="RitualOutcomeComp_ParticipantCount">
                <label>participant count</label>
                <curve>
                    <points>
                        <li>(1,  0.0)</li>
                        <li>(5,  0.3)</li>
                        <li>(10, 0.4)</li>
                    </points>
                </curve>
            </li>
        </comps>
        <outcomeChances>
            <li>
                <label>Fumbled</label>
                <chance>0.05</chance>
                <description>The {0} was a farce: the captive spat curses, the corruptor lost her focus, and the mana sputtered out before it could begin.</description>
                <positivityIndex>-2</positivityIndex>
            </li>
            <li>
                <label>Fizzled</label>
                <chance>0.15</chance>
                <description>The {0} was ineffective. The captive's body rejected the mana, and the rite guttered out like a dying candle.</description>
                <positivityIndex>-1</positivityIndex>
            </li>
            <li>
                <label>Overwhelming</label>
                <chance>0.6</chance>
                <description>The {0} was overwhelming. The captive's defiance dissolved as the mana remade her, cell by cell, into a monster.</description>
                <positivityIndex>1</positivityIndex>
            </li>
            <li>
                <label>Unstoppable</label>
                <chance>0.2</chance>
                <description>The {0} was unstoppable. The mana flooded through the captive in a single glorious surge, and a new monster opened her eyes.</description>
                <positivityIndex>2</positivityIndex>
            </li>
        </outcomeChances>
    </RitualOutcomeEffectDef>

    <!-- ===================== The meme ===================== -->

    <MemeDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
        <defName>ProjectMomo_Meme_MonsterExtremists</defName>
        <label>monster extremists</label>
        <description>All men should be drained, and all women should be transformed! The baseline human form is a larval state, unworthy of respect: women must be remade as monsters, and men must be claimed and drained by them. Only the ascended — monsters and their bonded mates — are truly worthy.</description>
        <iconPath>UI/Memes/Monsterbucker</iconPath>
        <groupDef>Misc</groupDef>
        <impact>2</impact>
        <!-- Mutually exclusive with FleshPurity and Transhumanist, which both
             carry this exclusion tag (the ascension precept also lists them as
             conflicting memes, as defense in depth). -->
        <exclusionTags>
            <li>FleshAugmentation</li>
        </exclusionTags>
        <requireOne>
            <li>
                <li>ProjectMomo_MonsterAscension_Relaxed</li>
                <li>ProjectMomo_MonsterAscension_Exalted</li>
                <li>ProjectMomo_MonsterAscension_Strict</li>
            </li>
            <li>
                <li>ProjectMomo_Ritual_TransformColonist</li>
            </li>
            <li>
                <li>ProjectMomo_Ritual_TransformCaptive</li>
            </li>
        </requireOne>
        <generalRules>
            <rulesStrings>
                <li>memeAdjective-&gt;monstrous</li>
                <li>memeAdjective-&gt;demon-touched</li>
                <li>memeAdjective-&gt;ascendant</li>
                <li>memeCreed-&gt;cult</li>
                <li>memeCreed-&gt;sisterhood</li>
                <li>memeHyphenPrefix-&gt;monstro</li>
                <li>memeHyphenPrefix-&gt;demon</li>
                <li>memeConcept-&gt;ascension</li>
                <li>memeConcept-&gt;the inma</li>
                <li>memeConcept-&gt;corruption</li>
                <li>memeConcept-&gt;monstrous rebirth</li>
                <li>memeLeaderNoun-&gt;matriarch</li>
                <li>memeLeaderNoun-&gt;corrupter</li>
                <li>memeLeaderAdjective-&gt;monstrous</li>
                <li>memeLeaderAdjective-&gt;ascendant</li>
                <li>memeMoralist-&gt;tempter</li>
                <li>memeMoralist-&gt;corrupter</li>
                <li>memeMoralist-&gt;recruiter</li>
            </rulesStrings>
        </generalRules>
        <descriptionMaker>
            <rules>
                <rulesStrings>
                    <!-- theist myth -->
                    <li>creation(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)        -&gt;[deity0_name] looked upon the first humans and found their bodies wanting, so [deity0_pronoun] remade the most beloved of them into monsters, beautiful and hungry, and bade them claim the rest.</li>
                    <li>episode(uses=1,tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)  -&gt;Those who clung to their baseline flesh were passed over by [deity0_name]'s blessing, and were forgotten.</li>
                    <!-- theist founder -->
                    <li>intro(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)           -&gt;On the [place_summary] [place_name] there was a [altarName] in [deity0_name]'s [altarRoomLabel], where the [deity0_type] poured mana into the willing and remade them.</li>
                    <li>conflict(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)        -&gt;A fearful [foeLeader] sent [foeSoldiers] to burn the monsters and keep everyone trapped in baseline flesh.</li>
                    <li>founderJoin(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)     -&gt;A [place_job] named [founderName] answered by offering [founder_possessive] own body to the mana, and rose from the ritual circle as something greater than human.</li>
                    <li>victory(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)         -&gt;The [foeLeader] finally sent [foeSoldiers] to destroy the [memberNamePlural], but the monsters' charm unraveled their resolve, and one by one they knelt to be remade.</li>
                    <!-- ideological founder -->
                    <li>setup(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)           -&gt;[founderName] watched a monster drain a man to blissful ruin and remake a woman in her own image, and understood at once what humanity was for.</li>
                    <li>story(uses=1,tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)    -&gt;[founderName] taught [founder_possessive] followers that the baseline form is only a chrysalis, and that clinging to it is cowardice.</li>
                    <!-- ideological lesson -->
                    <li>lessonIntro(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)     -&gt;The first sister I watched awaken wept with joy at what she had become, and in her tears I finally saw the truth we had all been missing:</li>
                    <li>lesson(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)          -&gt;to stay baseline is to refuse to be born</li>
                    <li>lessonReinforcement(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists) -&gt;It became so clear when my own hunger for essence first stirred, and I felt what I had always been meant to be.</li>
                    <!-- archist -->
                    <li>archistBasis(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)    -&gt;The archotechs themselves reshaped lesser beings to suit their designs; to remake the human form is to walk in their image.</li>
                    <li>archistFact(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)     -&gt;A body rewritten by mana is a perfected instrument, closer to the archotechs' flawless workings than any baseline flesh.</li>
                    <!-- animist -->
                    <li>animistBasis(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)    -&gt;Every soul carries a monster spirit sleeping within it; the rite of awakening merely lets the true spirit out.</li>
                    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_MonsterExtremists)     -&gt;Baseline flesh is a cage, and the spirits rejoice when it is opened.</li>
                </rulesStrings>
            </rules>
        </descriptionMaker>
